# ABOUTME: The notebook venv's top-level packages; requirements.txt is their full lock, every wheel by version and sha256.
# ABOUTME: Regenerate the lock with the command below and commit both; the Dockerfile installs only the lock (#1273).
#
#   uv pip compile images/web-terminal/requirements.in --python-version 3.11.18 \
#     --python-platform x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu --generate-hashes --only-binary :all: --no-header \
#     -o images/web-terminal/requirements.txt
#
# Python 3.11.18 is the python-build-standalone CPython the Dockerfile fetches by version and sha256 and builds the
# venv from (#1480); bookworm's own python3 is 3.11.2, older than soupsieve's floor below needs. Wheels only, so no
# build backend is fetched unhashed at build time. jupyterlab and jupyter-collaboration are held where the
# Dockerfile's comment says (collaboration 5.x needs jupyterlab>=4.6); the rest took the latest release that resolved
# on 2026-11-09.
# On 2026-11-16 (#1475) jupyterlab moved to 4.6.6, the latest 4.6.x, past the advisories that end at 4.6.3, and the
# tornado floor below holds jupyter-server's tornado past its advisory (6.6.0 and before) when the lock is regenerated.
# On 2026-11-16 (#1480) the venv's interpreter moved to 3.11.18, and the soupsieve floor below holds nbconvert's and
# beautifulsoup4's soupsieve past its advisories (fixed in 3.0.2 and 4.0.0), releases that need Python 3.11.5 or later.
jupyterlab==4.6.6
jupyter-collaboration==5.0.1
jupyter-resource-usage
jupyterlab-git
jupyterlab_execute_time
ipywidgets
boto3
tornado>=6.6.1
soupsieve>=4.0.0
# pip itself, in place of the upgrade to whatever was latest that the venv used to take.
pip
